        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00610/" ed="1r" type="sheet"/>
          <lb/>LINES TO DR. WALTER BIRK ON HIS RETIRING FROM GENERAL PRACTICE
          <lb/>When yeu first arrived in Kirchstetten, trains had
          <lb/>long been taken for granted, but electric
          <lb/>licht was still a surprise and as yet no ene
          <lb/>had seen a tracter.

          <lb/>Te-day,after forty-five years, as yeu leave us,
          <lb/>autebahns are a must, nid-wives are banished
          <lb/>and village decters become museum pieces
          <lb/>like the horse-and-buggy.

          <lb/>I regret. The specialist has his function
          <lb/>but, to him, we are merely wanal examples of
          <lb/>what he knows all abeut. The healer I faith is
          <lb/>someone I've gessiped
        
          <lb/>and drunk with before I call him te teuch me,
          <lb/>one whe admits hew easy it is to (misconster)
          <lb/>what our bedies are trying te say, for each one
          <lb/>talks in a local

          <lb/>dialect of its own which can alter during
          <lb/>its life-time: so children run hich fevers on
          <lb/>slight prevecation, while the ergans of old men
          <lb/>suffer in silence.

          <lb/>When summer plumps again, eur usual sparrews
          <lb/>will phip in the eaves of the patulous chesnuts
          <lb/>near your old hene, but nene will ask -"Is Docter
          <lb/>Birk areund te hear me?".,
        
          <lb/>for nething can happen te birds that has net
          <lb/>happened before: we theuch are beasts with a sense of
          <lb/>real occasion,of beginnings and endings,
          <lb/>which is the reasen

          <lb/>we like te keep eur clocks punctual, as Nature's
          <lb/>never is. Seasons She has but ne Calendar,
          <lb/>fer every year the strawberries ripen
          <lb/>and the autuan crecus

          <lb/>lane  inte blessem en unpredictable
          <lb/>dates. But Such Schlamperei cannet be allewed an
          <lb/>histerian: for us it's a matter of hener
          <lb/>te keep eur birth-days

          <lb/>and wedding-days, to rejeice er to neurn, en
          <lb/>the right ene. Henceforth the First of Octeber
          <lb/>shall be special for yeu and us, as the ence when
          <lb/>you quit the Public
        
          <lb/>Realm te private yeur ways and (smudge in a quiet 
          <lb/>yeu so deserve. Farewell, and de net Wince at
          <lb/>eur sick werld: it is genuine in age to be
          <lb/>happily selfish.
        
        <lb/> ____



        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00611/" ed="1v" type="sheet"/>
